WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.600
Your salary is on hold, confirm

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.094
within twenty-four hours.

3
00:00:04.474 --> 00:00:06.490
A message like this wants you

4
00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:08.116
to act before you think.

5
00:00:09.066 --> 00:00:10.854
Look for the warning signs.

6
00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:12.632
Pressure to act fast.

7
00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:14.638
A link you didn't expect.

8
00:00:15.018 --> 00:00:16.644
A sender you can't check.

9
00:00:17.024 --> 00:00:19.616
And a request for your PIN or a code.

10
00:00:19.996 --> 00:00:22.510
No real payroll office asks for those.

11
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.750
So here's the habit.

12
00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:26.984
Don't tap the link or reply.

13
00:00:27.364 --> 00:00:28.828
Call the office on a

14
00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.388
number you already have.

15
00:00:30.768 --> 00:00:33.240
Never share a PIN or a one-time code.

16
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.032
Then report the message, warn your

17
00:00:36.032 --> 00:00:37.646
colleagues and delete it.

18
00:00:38.596 --> 00:00:39.268
Your turn.

19
00:00:39.648 --> 00:00:42.516
A colleague's number writes: I sent you a

20
00:00:42.516 --> 00:00:44.928
code by mistake, please forward it.

21
00:00:45.308 --> 00:00:46.208
Scam or safe?

22
00:00:47.158 --> 00:00:49.222
Remember: phishing pretends to

23
00:00:49.222 --> 00:00:50.620
be someone you trust.

24
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.932
Spot the sign, stop, and

25
00:00:52.932 --> 00:00:54.102
check another way.

26
00:00:54.482 --> 00:00:56.444
Then report it and delete it.
